<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <Import Project="../UnityReferenceAssemblies.props" />
  <!--
    A LOCAL TYPE-CHECKER for the package's EDITMODE test sources (#616), and the fourth and last of
    the source trees this repository ships.

    Why this exists. Three check projects existed and between them they missed one tree:
    `TypeCheck` compiles `Runtime/**`, `EditorCheck` compiles `Runtime/**` + `Editor/**`, and
    `TestCheck` compiles `Runtime/**` + `Tests/Core/**` + `Tests/Runtime/**`. NOTHING compiled
    `Tests/Editor/**` - 655 files across 28 feature-scoped assemblies - so an editmode fixture was
    type-checked by exactly one thing, a Unity matrix leg roughly fifty minutes away. It has been
    paid for: `WPROTO044` on `FloatListCache` in
    `Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/TestTypes/NestedCollectionSerializationTypes.cs` (#613) was the one
    instance of that diagnostic in the repository no local gate could see, and it cost its own CI
    round. The same hole applied to every `WPROTO###` and `WUH###` the package ships and to ordinary
    `CS####` in an editor fixture.

    It compiles the REAL sources against the REAL analyzers - both shipped assemblies, the way
    TypeCheck, EditorCheck and TestCheck do - so a diagnostic fires here exactly as it does in the
    editor. It is a type-checker, not a test runner. Nothing here executes.

    ======================= WHY A FOURTH PROJECT AND NOT A WIDER THIRD =======================

    `TestCheck` cannot take this tree: it references only the community `UnityEngine.Modules`, and
    every editmode fixture binds `UnityEditor`.

    `EditorCheck` could, and must not. It EXCLUDES seven files under `Editor/` for reasons that are
    the harness's rather than the author's - two permanent uGUI ones, three driven by the
    `Unity3D.SDK` 2021.1.14 pin, two cascades of those. An editmode fixture binding one of those
    seven excluded types then fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the fixture, and mixing
    the two trees in one project makes the two kinds of red indistinguishable at a glance. Kept
    apart, `typecheck:editor` red means the EDITOR sources broke and `typecheck:editor-tests` red
    means the FIXTURES did - and the cascade of EditorCheck's exclusions lands in one clearly
    labelled block of this file rather than being smeared through EditorCheck's.

    ================================ WHAT IT COMPILES ================================

    614 of the 655 files under `Tests/Editor/`, plus the four trees they bind:

      * `Runtime/**` and `Editor/**`, with TypeCheck's and EditorCheck's exclusions, because every
        editmode asmdef references `WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers` and all but three reference
        `WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.Editor`. TypeCheck and EditorCheck remain the gates that JUDGE
        those two trees; a divergence here is a bug in one of the three.
      * `Tests/Core/**` INCLUDING `Tests/Core/Editor/**`. `TestCheck` excludes that last directory
        because it has no `UnityEditor` to compile it with, so those four fixtures were in the same
        hole this project closes; here they are in scope, which is why they appear in the governed
        asmdef list `lint-typecheck-asmdef-references` prints.
      * `Tests/Runtime/TestTypes/**` and `Tests/Runtime/TestDoubles/**`, and NOT the rest of
        `Tests/Runtime/**`. Four editmode asmdefs reference the `WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.Tests.Runtime`
        assembly, and measured across the tree they bind exactly two namespaces out of it:
        `Tests.Runtime.TestTypes.*` (the eleven Odin drawer and WButton inspector fixtures) and
        `Tests.AssetProcessors` (the `TestDetectableAsset` / `ITestDetectableContract` doubles the
        AssetProcessors fixtures derive from). Compiling the WHOLE PlayMode tree here would add
        nothing `TestCheck` does not already judge and would collide on its own: `HelpersTests` is
        declared as a partial class with a DIFFERENT base in `Tests/Runtime/Helper/` and
        `Tests/Editor/Helper/`, which Unity compiles into two assemblies and one assembly cannot.

    The sources compile into ONE assembly with the runtime's own name, which is what makes the
    fixtures' `internal` access resolve without reproducing the package's InternalsVisibleTo graph.

    ============================== ONLY TWO CONFIGURATIONS ==============================

    Its three siblings each build four define configurations. This one builds TWO, and the two it
    drops are dropped on a measurement rather than for speed:

      * DEFAULT and ODIN ship. Odin is not optional here: `Tests/Editor/**` names
        `WALLSTOP_UNITY_HELPERS_ODIN_INSPECTOR` at 158 sites across more than a hundred files, and
        `Tests/Editor/Utils/Odin/`'s asmdef carries it as a `defineConstraints` entry, so the
        define-off build compiles a materially different tree from the define-on one. This is #347's
        argument one level down: before this project, the editmode Odin FIXTURES compiled nowhere in
        automation, exactly as the editor Odin DRAWERS did not.
      * `WallstopProto=false` and `SINGLE_THREADED` do NOT. `Tests/Editor/**` contains zero
        `WALLSTOP_PROTO` preprocessor uses and zero `SINGLE_THREADED` ones - the only two matches for
        the latter are prose in a comment in `ScriptableObjectSingletonCreatorEditorTests.cs`. The
        `Runtime/**` and `Editor/**` trees compiled here as dependencies DO branch on both, and both
        branches are already judged in those configurations by `typecheck:unity` and
        `typecheck:editor`. Two more builds of this project would re-compile what two other projects
        already compile and add no fixture coverage at all. The day an editmode fixture grows either
        branch, the missing configuration belongs back in `package.json` next to `:odin`.

    ================================ THE REFERENCE ASSEMBLIES ================================

    Both pins are inherited rather than invented: the engine half is `UnityEngine.Modules` 2021.3.33
    from `../UnityReferenceAssemblies.props`, and the editor half is EditorCheck's `Unity3D.SDK`
    2021.1.14 - TWO MINOR VERSIONS BELOW the package's 2021.3 support floor, and unmovable, because
    2021.1.14.1 is the newest version that package has ever published. Read a red from this project
    the way #553 taught us to read one from TypeCheck: a confident RED for a Unity nobody ships is
    the worse failure mode, because nothing in a compiler error says which Unity answered. Before
    "fixing" any error this project reports against a `UnityEditor` or `UnityEngine` member, confirm
    the member's availability floor - and if the member is present in a real 2021.3 editor, the file
    belongs on the exclusion list below rather than in a changed source file.

    ============================ WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER ============================

    41 of the 655 files under `Tests/Editor/` are excluded, in FOUR groups, every one of them
    removed ONE PER LINE WITH ITS REASON below rather than through a semicolon-packed `Exclude`, so
    each reason travels with the exclusion it explains. Not one of them is excluded because the
    fixture is wrong:

      1. The 7 DI-integration fixtures under `Tests/Editor/Integrations/`. Their asmdefs carry
         `REFLEX_PRESENT` / `VCONTAINER_PRESENT` / `ZENJECT_PRESENT` define constraints and bind
         third-party containers with no NuGet equivalent in this graph, exactly as
         `Runtime/Integrations/**` and `Tests/Runtime/Integrations/**` are out of the other three
         projects' scope.
      2. 22 files that CASCADE off EditorCheck's pin-driven exclusion of
         `Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer.cs` and
         `Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetPropertyDrawer.cs`. Those two production files read the
         GETTER of `SerializedProperty.managedReferenceValue`, which Unity added after 2021.1: the
         reference assembly carries the setter alone, so the read is CS0154. This is the trap #616
         predicted, and it is the single largest gap in this gate - see the note under the block.
      3. 10 files that bind `Texture2D.alphaIsTransparency`, an EDITOR-ONLY member of
         `UnityEngine.Texture2D`. `UnityEngine.Modules` publishes the PLAYER reference assemblies, so
         the member is absent here and present in every editor, including 2021.3. Six bind it
         directly; four are pure cascades of the two shared fixtures among those six.
      4. 2 files that bind `FitTextureSizeWindow`, which EditorCheck excludes because
         `TextureImporter.GetSourceTextureWidthAndHeight` postdates 2021.1.

    Also not covered, deliberately:

      * PlayMode fixtures beyond the two directories named above. `TestCheck` is their gate.
      * The test framework's BEHAVIOUR. `UnityEngine.TestTools` and `UnityEditor.TestTools` ship with
        com.unity.test-framework and have no NuGet equivalent, so the shims declare the members these
        fixtures bind: enough to type-check a call and nothing more.
      * Anything resolved out of Unity's own METADATA rather than a signature - attribute targets,
        parameter defaults, serialization behaviour, drawer registration. See #553.
      * IL2CPP and behaviour. A green build here is necessary and NOT sufficient; the Unity editmode
        legs remain the real proof.

    THE ONE GAP WORTH REOPENING. Group 2 costs this gate the whole `SerializableDictionary` /
    `SerializableSet` drawer fixture suite, and it is not fixable from inside this project: no shim
    can stand in for those two drawers the way `Shims/ValidationSharedShim.cs` stands in for
    `ValidationShared`, because the fixtures bind roughly 130 distinct members and nested types
    across them and a shim that drifts from 18,000 lines of real drawer would hand back a confident
    GREEN, which is worse than the red it replaced. Both this group and group 4 evaporate the day a
    `UnityEditor` reference assembly newer than 2021.1.14 exists on nuget.org; until then the only
    other way to close them is a real editor, which is what the Unity editmode legs already are.

    NoWarn is EditorCheck's set plus one:

      * CS0169, "field is never used", alongside the CS0649 that is already there for the same
        reason: `Tests/Editor/TestTypes/BackingFieldGroupAsset.cs` declares
        `[SerializeField] private int _outside`, a field Unity serializes and C# cannot see used.
        The real Unity build judges these; here they are noise.
      * CS0436, CS1701 and NU1701 are the three harness artifacts EditorCheck's header enumerates -
        the DoesNotReturnAttribute polyfill under UNITY_2021, `UnityEditor.dll`'s
        `UnityEngine 0.0.0.0` reference binding to the facade, and `Unity3D.SDK`'s bare `lib/` folder.

    Like its three siblings this project lives under `Generator~`, which Unity ignores by the
    trailing-tilde convention, and ships to nobody.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.1</TargetFramework>
    <!-- Unity 2021.3, the oldest version in the CI matrix, is the constraint that matters. -->
    <LangVersion>9</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
    <!-- The runtime's own name, as in TestCheck: the fixtures are `internal`-visible to it by
         being it. -->
    <AssemblyName>WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers</RootNamespace>
    <RepoRoot>$([System.IO.Path]::GetFullPath('$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/../..'))</RepoRoot>
    <!-- EditorCheck's editor pin, restated rather than shared because the two projects are the only
         two that hold it and a silent drift between them would be invisible. See the header. -->
    <UnityEditorReferenceAssemblyVersion>2021.1.14.1</UnityEditorReferenceAssemblyVersion>
    <!-- WyRandom uses a pointer for its state mixing. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <!-- Unity defines this in every test assembly, every editmode asmdef here carries it as a
         `defineConstraints` entry, and the package gates test-only internals on it. -->
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);UNITY_INCLUDE_TESTS</DefineConstants>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS0414;CS0649;CS0169;CS0219;CS0618;CS0612;CS1591;CS1573</NoWarn>
    <!-- The three harness artifacts EditorCheck enumerates. Each is one diagnostic with one named
         cause, not a category swept under the rug. -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS0436;CS1701;NU1701</NoWarn>
    <WallstopProto Condition="'$(WallstopProto)' == ''">true</WallstopProto>
    <DefineConstants Condition="'$(WallstopProto)' == 'true'"
      >$(DefineConstants);WALLSTOP_PROTO</DefineConstants>
    <!-- The configuration that earns its build here. See the header. -->
    <WallstopOdin Condition="'$(WallstopOdin)' == ''">false</WallstopOdin>
    <DefineConstants Condition="'$(WallstopOdin)' == 'true'"
      >$(DefineConstants);WALLSTOP_UNITY_HELPERS_ODIN_INSPECTOR</DefineConstants>
    <!-- Declared but not built by any npm script, for the reason the header gives: no fixture under
         `Tests/Editor/**` branches on it. Left switchable so the day one does, the configuration is
         a `-p:` away rather than a csproj edit. -->
    <WallstopSingleThreaded Condition="'$(WallstopSingleThreaded)' == ''"
      >false</WallstopSingleThreaded>
    <DefineConstants Condition="'$(WallstopSingleThreaded)' == 'true'"
      >$(DefineConstants);SINGLE_THREADED</DefineConstants>
    <!--
      The switch the probe half of `lint:typecheck-asmdef-references` throws (#598). Unity compiles
      each asmdef separately and every test asmdef here sets `overrideReferences: true`, so its
      `precompiledReferences` are the complete list its sources may bind; this project compiles 28 of
      them into one assembly with one reference list. Three of the assemblies below are needed by
      `Runtime/**` alone and named by NO governed asmdef, so they are held behind this switch and the
      probe drops them to ask the compiler the one question reading files cannot: does any fixture
      use them? Errors inside `Runtime/**` are expected there; an error in a fixture is the drift.
    -->
    <WallstopRuntimeOnlyReferences Condition="'$(WallstopRuntimeOnlyReferences)' == ''"
      >true</WallstopRuntimeOnlyReferences>
    <!--
      UNITY_EDITOR plus the symbol set a real Unity 2021.3 editor defines, identical to EditorCheck's.
      These are not decoration: `Editor/Tools/UnityMethodAnalyzer/*` branches on bare `UNITY_2021`,
      so does the DoesNotReturnAttribute polyfill in Runtime/Core/Serialization, and the editmode
      fixtures live behind `UNITY_EDITOR` end to end.
    -->
    <UnityVersionDefines>UNITY_2021;UNITY_2021_3;UNITY_2021_3_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2021_2_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2021_1_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2020_3_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2020_2_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2020_1_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2019_4_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2019_1_OR_NEWER;UNITY_2018_1_OR_NEWER;UNITY_5_3_OR_NEWER</UnityVersionDefines>
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);UNITY_EDITOR;$(UnityVersionDefines)</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- THE VERSION UNITY SHIPS, exactly, for TestCheck's reason (#495): a gate compiled against a
         newer NUnit binds members no Unity leg has. -->
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit" Version="3.5.0" NoWarn="NU1701" />
    <!-- ExcludeAssets="all" because only lib/UnityEditor.dll is wanted; the package's own
         UnityEngine.dll must NOT be referenced alongside the UnityEngine.Modules facade.
         GeneratePathProperty is what makes $(PkgUnity3D_SDK) resolvable below. -->
    <PackageReference
      Include="Unity3D.SDK"
      Version="$(UnityEditorReferenceAssemblyVersion)"
      GeneratePathProperty="true"
      ExcludeAssets="all"
      NoWarn="NU1701"
    />
    <!-- The analyzer Unity actually loads, so a contract the generator refuses fails HERE. It is
         also a source generator the runtime cannot compile without. -->
    <Analyzer Include="$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Analyzers/WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.Proto.Generator.dll" />
    <!-- The general-purpose WUH### analyzers ship in the same folder and Unity loads both,
         so both have to be loaded here or a local gate covers less than the editor does. -->
    <Analyzer Include="$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Analyzers/WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.Analyzers.dll" />
    <CompilerVisibleProperty Include="WProtoDisableModuleInitializer" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The editor half. Private=false: nothing is deployed, this project only type-checks. -->
    <Reference Include="UnityEditor">
      <HintPath>$(PkgUnity3D_SDK)/lib/UnityEditor.dll</HintPath>
      <Private>false</Private>
    </Reference>
    <!-- Declared by six of the 28 governed asmdefs and needed by `Runtime/**`. Held unconditionally,
         and recorded in the linter's UNDECLARED_BY_DESIGN, because SOME governed asmdef declares it:
         the probe's job is the assemblies NONE of them declare. -->
    <Reference Include="System.Text.Json">
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Binaries/System.Text.Json.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <!-- Needed by `Runtime/**`; declared by `Tests.Runtime`, whose TestTypes/TestDoubles this
         project compiles, and by no editmode asmdef - and no editmode fixture names ProtoBuf,
         ImmutableArray, or any type out of these three. -->
    <Reference Include="protobuf-net">
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Protobuf-Net/protobuf-net.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <Reference Include="protobuf-net.Core">
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Protobuf-Net/protobuf-net.Core.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <Reference Include="System.Collections.Immutable">
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Protobuf-Net/System.Collections.Immutable.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <!--
      RUNTIME-ONLY, and switchable for that reason - the same three TestCheck holds behind the same
      switch. NO governed asmdef declares any of them, so nothing under `Tests/**` may bind them;
      `Runtime/**` needs all three and its asmdef auto-references every bundled plugin.
    -->
    <Reference
      Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Unsafe"
      Condition="'$(WallstopRuntimeOnlyReferences)' == 'true'"
    >
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Protobuf-Net/System.Runtime.CompilerServices.Unsafe.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <Reference
      Include="System.Text.Encodings.Web"
      Condition="'$(WallstopRuntimeOnlyReferences)' == 'true'"
    >
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Binaries/System.Text.Encodings.Web.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <Reference
      Include="Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces"
      Condition="'$(WallstopRuntimeOnlyReferences)' == 'true'"
    >
      <HintPath>$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Binaries/Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces.dll</HintPath>
    </Reference>
    <!--
      `System.IO.Pipelines` is deliberately absent, as it now is from all three siblings: it is a
      transitive dependency of System.Text.Json that no source in any tree binds, and holding a
      reference nothing needs only widens the gap between this gate and Unity (#598).
    -->
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- TypeCheck's shims: the ModuleInitializer polyfill, the uGUI ColorBlock, and the
         runtime-side Odin base classes. Split on the Odin define for TestCheck's reason - an
         unconditional glob would let an UNGUARDED `Sirenix.OdinInspector` reference in a fixture
         bind and pass in the define-off configuration, which is CS0246 in a real project. -->
    <Compile
      Include="../WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.TypeCheck/Shims/*.cs"
      Exclude="../WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.TypeCheck/Shims/OdinInspectorShim.cs"
    />
    <Compile
      Include="../WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.TypeCheck/Shims/OdinInspectorShim.cs"
      Condition="'$(WallstopOdin)' == 'true'"
    />
    <!-- EditorCheck's shims: UI Toolkit drag events, the Test Runner API, the prefab-stage types
         that moved namespace in 2021.2, and the ValidationShared stand-in the editor drawers and
         the fixtures that name them both need. -->
    <Compile Include="../WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.EditorCheck/Shims/*.cs" />
    <Compile
      Include="../WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.EditorCheck/ShimsOdin/*.cs"
      Condition="'$(WallstopOdin)' == 'true'"
    />
    <!-- TestCheck's shim: the com.unity.test-framework members the fixtures bind. -->
    <Compile Include="../WallstopStudios.UnityHelpers.TestCheck/Shims/*.cs" />
    <!-- The runtime, with TypeCheck's exclusions. TypeCheck remains the gate that JUDGES it. -->
    <Compile
      Include="$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/**/*.cs"
      Exclude="$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Integrations/**/*.cs;$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Analyzers/**/*.cs;$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Core/Extension/Partials/UI.cs;$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Utils/MatchColliderToSprite.cs;$(RepoRoot)/Runtime/Visuals/UGUI/EnhancedImage.cs"
    />
    <!-- The editor sources, with EditorCheck's seven exclusions, restated one per line so the
         cascade block further down can name the file each fixture is waiting on. EditorCheck
         remains the gate that JUDGES this tree; its header carries the full reasoning. -->
    <Compile Include="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/**/*.cs" />
    <!-- PERMANENT. Binds `Visuals.UGUI.EnhancedImage` and `UnityEditor.UI.ImageEditor`; uGUI
         (com.unity.ugui) ships as a Unity package with no NuGet equivalent on either side. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/Visuals/EnhancedImageEditor.cs" />
    <!-- PERMANENT. Binds `MatchColliderToSprite`, uGUI-dependent and already out of the Runtime set. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/CustomEditors/MatchColliderToSpriteEditor.cs" />
    <!-- PIN-DRIVEN. `AssetDatabase.SaveAssetIfDirty`, absent from Unity3D.SDK 2021.1.14 and present
         in 2021.3. Stood in for by EditorCheck's `Shims/AnimationEventEditorShim.cs`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/AnimationEventEditor.cs" />
    <!-- PIN-DRIVEN. `TextureImporter.GetSourceTextureWidthAndHeight`, same shape. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/FitTextureSizeWindow.cs" />
    <!-- PIN-DRIVEN. Reads the GETTER of `SerializedProperty.managedReferenceValue` at three sites;
         2021.1.14 carries the setter alone, so the read is CS0154. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer.cs" />
    <!-- PIN-DRIVEN, and stood in for by EditorCheck's `Shims/ValidationSharedShim.cs`, which mirrors
         its surface so the files that only NAME it keep compiling. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/CustomDrawers/Utils/ValidationShared.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY. Names `SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer` and
         `SerializableCollectionTweenDiagnostics`, both declared in the file removed above. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetPropertyDrawer.cs" />
    <!-- The shared test utilities every editmode asmdef references, INCLUDING `Tests/Core/Editor/**`,
         which TestCheck cannot compile for want of a UnityEditor. -->
    <Compile
      Include="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Core/**/*.cs"
      Exclude="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Core/TestUtils/CiTestResultStreamLogger.cs"
    />
    <!-- The two PlayMode directories the editmode fixtures actually bind, and no more. See the
         header for why the rest of `Tests/Runtime/**` is TestCheck's alone. -->
    <Compile Include="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Runtime/TestTypes/**/*.cs" />
    <Compile Include="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Runtime/TestDoubles/**/*.cs" />
    <!--
      The tree this project exists for: 614 of the 655 files under `Tests/Editor/`. GROUP 1 of the
      four exclusion groups is the only one expressed as an `Exclude`, because it is a whole
      directory with one reason rather than a list of files with their own.
    -->
    <Compile
      Include="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/**/*.cs"
      Exclude="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/Integrations/**/*.cs"
    />
    <!--
      GROUP 2, 22 files: CASCADE ONLY off the two editor drawers removed above, which are themselves
      out because `SerializedProperty.managedReferenceValue` has no getter in Unity3D.SDK 2021.1.14.
      Nothing is wrong with any of these fixtures and none of them can be shimmed back in - see THE
      ONE GAP WORTH REOPENING in the header. Each line names which of the two drawers it binds.
    -->
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableSetPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/EditorDrawerStaticStyleInitializationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/NestedCollectionSerializationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/ScriptableSingletonSerializationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableCollectionChildHeightSignalTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableCollectionDrawerVisualRegressionTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableCollectionIndentAlignmentTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableCollectionPaginationHeightTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableCollectionPendingFoldoutInteractionTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableCollectionTweenAnimationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableDictionaryIndentationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableDictionaryPendingPaddingTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer`. The largest single loss in this
         gate at 5,600 lines, and the reason the header proposes reopening the group rather than
         leaving it. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawerTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawerUndoTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetAnimationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableSetPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetDangerWarningTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableSetPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetIndentationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableSetPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetPendingPaddingTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableSetPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetPropertyDrawerTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableSetPropertyDrawer`. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/SerializableSetPropertyDrawerUndoTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names both drawers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/CustomDrawers/WGroupSerializableCollectionIntegrationTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer` at two sites. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/Settings/SettingsSerializedObjectCacheTests.cs" />
    <!-- CASCADE ONLY: names `SerializableDictionaryPropertyDrawer` at one site. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/Settings/UnityHelpersSettingsTests.cs" />
    <!--
      GROUP 3, 10 files: `Texture2D.alphaIsTransparency`. That member exists only in the EDITOR's
      UnityEngine.dll, and `UnityEngine.Modules` publishes the PLAYER reference assemblies, so it
      reads as absent here and is present in every editor the package supports - including 2021.3.
      HARNESS GAP, not a package one, and not a pin that can be moved: UnityEngine.Modules has
      published exactly one version.
    -->
    <!-- Sets `alphaIsTransparency` in three object initializers. -->
    <Compile Remove="$(RepoRoot)/Tests/Editor/Sprites/Cropper/SpriteCropperAdditionalTests.cs" />
    <!-- Sets `alphaIsTransparency` in one object initializer. -->
